## https://www.queensu.ca/admission/applicants/english-proficiency 200 https://www.queensu.ca/admission/applicants/english-proficiency
- Test Minimum Scores Share Your Results With International English Language Testing System (IELTS) A score of 6.5 on Academic Module with no band below 6.0 Queens University – Undergrad Admission through IELTS Test of English as a Foreign Language (TOEFL) Institution Code: 0949 TOEFL (Home Edition) 4.5 overall with no skill lower than 4.0.
- 88 overall, minimum 20 on Writing, Speaking, Reading and Listening (Before January 2026) Institution Code 0949 through TOEFL Canadian Academic English Language Assessment (CAEL) Overall band of 70 with no band below 60 Queen’s University through CAEL Queen’s School of English Successful completion of QBridge Programming Pearson Test of English Academic (PTE Academic) Overall score of 60 Queen’s University through PTE Duolingo English Test Minimum score 120 The Duolingo English Test is an online 
- Queen’s University through Duolingo Cambridge English 175, with no component below 170 Queen’s University through Cambridge LanguageCert Academic 70, with no individual score below 65 Queen’s University through LanguageCert Academic English Language Proficiency test results are valid for a maximum of two years before beginning studies at Queen's.
- Term QBridge Accelerated (QBA) English for Academic Purposes (EAP) Fall (September start | Winter (January start) Entry requirements: IELTS: 6.0 overall Cambridge English : 170 TOEFL : iBT 80 CAEL: Overall Band 60 or equivalent Duolingo : 95 PTE : 55 MELAB : 78 LanguageCert Academic : Minimum band score of 65 Graduated Entry-exit requirements: B+ in ESLA 140 (Advanced level), or B- in ESLA 150 (University Preparation level) Exit requirements*: a final grade of B at the end of the summer program 
- If we determine that you still need to provide an English language test score, you must submit an acceptable result by March 31st.
